;;;; cpu-ki-teacher.lisp — the KI matchup's neutral by the offline teacher's table (docs/duel/DUEL_AI_TEACHER.md §8; the user,
;;;; 2026-11-08: 「A」, the pilot in this pairing only; 「全部用老師，並加強 HARD」, the form in the key: 「分類加上型態、重算表再上線」). When a KI fighter's CPU is free (idle or running) and not about to awaken, it looks up
;;;; its situation as it perceives it (its character, the perceived distance band, the opponent's perceived state: the SNAP, so the
;;;; difficulty's perception delay *AI-DELAY* is its reaction time), keeps only the actions within the difficulty's mistake budget of the
;;;; best, and draws one by a softmax at the difficulty's temperature (readable: low temperatures, the same cue the same behaviour). Its
;;;; press is the CPU's own (AI-PRESS); a wait / guard / walk holds 20 frames (the commitment). Everything else (moves, combos, stun, wake-up,
;;;; the awakening, an unseen situation) stays the matchup style CPU's (cpu-ki-ken.lisp, cpu-ki-ichigo.lisp).
(in-package :duel)

(defparameter *kt-actions* '(:j1 :sp :hoho :step-in :step-out :step-side :guard :wait :walk-in :walk-out)
  "The teacher's macro actions, in its table's order (DUEL_AI_TEACHER §6).")
(defparameter *kt-tau* '(:easy 0.05 :normal 0.03 :hard 0.015) "Softmax temperature per difficulty (value units: Konpaku), 2026-11-08.")
(defparameter *kt-budget* '(:easy 0.10 :normal 0.05 :hard 0.02) "Mistake budget per difficulty: actions worse than the best by more never drawn.")
(defparameter *kt-on* '(:kenpachi :ichigo) "Characters whose KI neutral is the teacher's (a tool may narrow it to compare one side).")
(defparameter *kt-off-at* '((:kenpachi :hard))
  "(character difficulty) pairs left on the matchup style CPU: Kenpachi's HARD (his teacher won 4 of 40 against Ichigo's HARD style CPU,
